Z||000000||vinnywolfe||06-25-2000||11:22 PM||||i was working on an 87 GT that i am kinda' restoring today when i went to replace the driver's side coolant pipe.  the car had been in an accident on that side and the person i bought the car off of just cut the broken piece of pipe off and ran a long rubber coolant hose in it's place.  anyway, the old piece of pipe was hard to get off, especially around the front. i ended up cutting it to remove it. it took me 2 hours to wrestle the new one on and i still ended up putting a couple dings in it.  all the bends and crap that you have to go around, there has to be an easier way to do this.<BR>thanks.<BR>vinny||||reg||1
